A.3 magnitude criterion: chi-bound, per-link translation, feasibility
==============================================================================
  Axiom 2 bound on the between-arm experienced-chi gap at fixed P:
  |dchi| <= eps*sigma*|f(d+0.05) - f(d)|  (trapped vs mobile)
    held P=    powerless: chi-bound=0.0308  linear-translation=0.0259 rating units  3x=0.0778
    held P=     moderate: chi-bound=0.0584  linear-translation=0.0490 rating units  3x=0.1471
    held P=     powerful: chi-bound=0.0886  linear-translation=0.0744 rating units  3x=0.2233
    held P=    organized: chi-bound=0.0886  linear-translation=0.0744 rating units  3x=0.2233
    held P=institutional: chi-bound=0.0390  linear-translation=0.0328 rating units  3x=0.0983
  Declared linear instrument resolution (7-point): 0.1667 rating units
  Max linear-translated bound over positions: 0.0744  (3x: 0.2233)
  ASSERT PASS: the 1x bound sits below one 7-point scale step at EVERY held
  position -- at 1x the magnitude criterion decides nothing at a realistic
  7-point instrument (any observed gap is within one scale step of the bound).
  The 3x-inflated bound CROSSES one scale step at mid-slope positions ['organized', 'powerful']:
  the feasibility verdict itself flips inside the 1x-3x band, which is why
  the 3x safety factor is REGISTERED AS ARBITRARY and the 1x-3x band
  DECLARED INDETERMINATE -- the indeterminacy is live, not academic.

  Threshold-link breaker (assertion iv): a sub-bound chi gap straddling theta
    dchi = 0.002 (<< bound 0.0886) -> rating gap = 1.0 (full scale)
  ASSERT PASS: the threshold link maps an arbitrarily small chi gap to a
  full-scale rating gap -- the magnitude criterion BREAKS under a saturating
  link. STATED LIMIT confirmed: the criterion is licensed only under an
  approximately linear reporting channel (the paper owes that sentence).

